## 7. Sequence Diagrams

### Sequence 1: User Login & Session Establishment

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Trader (Browser)
    participant UI as Login Page (login.php)
    participant Auth as Auth Controller
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / SQLite
    participant Session as PHP Session Store

    User->>UI: Enter Email & Password
    UI->>Auth: POST /login.php (credentials, csrf_token)
    Auth->>Auth: Verify CSRF token
    Auth->>DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = :email
    DB-->>Auth: Return user record (hash, id, username)
    Auth->>Auth: password_verify(password, hash)
    
    alt Invalid Password / User Not Found
        Auth-->>UI: Redirect with error: "Invalid credentials"
        UI-->>User: Show red alert banner
    else Valid Credentials
        Auth->>Session: session_regenerate_id(true)
        Auth->>Session: Store user_id, username, permissions
        Auth->>DB: UPDATE users SET last_login = NOW() WHERE id = :id
        Auth-->>UI: 302 Redirect to index.php
        UI-->>User: Render Dashboard with user greeting
    end
```

---

### Sequence 2: Stock Analysis & Technical Indicator Computation

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Trader (Browser)
    participant Page as stock_analysis.php
    participant API as api/stock_analysis.php
    participant Py as python/stock_data.py
    participant YF as Yahoo Finance Cloud

    User->>Page: Type Symbol (e.g. RELIANCE.NS) & Submit
    Page->>API: AJAX GET /api/stock_analysis.php?symbol=RELIANCE.NS
    API->>Py: exec(python stock_data.py --analysis RELIANCE.NS)
    Py->>YF: yfinance.Ticker('RELIANCE.NS').history(period='1y')
    YF-->>Py: Return 1-Year Daily OHLCV Bars
    Py->>Py: Compute RSI(14), MACD(12,26,9), SMA(20,50,200), EMA
    Py->>Py: Compute Support/Resistance, Valuation & Sentiment
    Py-->>API: Emit Structured JSON
    API-->>Page: Return JSON payload
    Page->>Page: Chart.js renders price & indicator charts
    Page-->>User: Display Technical Gauges & Quantitative Verdict
```

---

### Sequence 3: Virtual Buy Order with Stop-Loss Configuration

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Trader (Browser)
    participant Buy as buy.php
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / SQLite
    participant Py as python/stock_data.py
    participant YF as Yahoo Finance Cloud

    User->>Buy: Input Symbol 'TCS.NS' & Qty 5
    Buy->>Py: Fetch live market price
    Py->>YF: yf.Ticker('TCS.NS').fast_info['last_price']
    YF-->>Py: Live Price = ₹3,500.00
    Py-->>Buy: Quote = ₹3,500.00
    User->>Buy: Set Stop-Loss = 5% (₹3,325.00) & Click Submit
    
    Buy->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    Buy->>DB: SELECT balance FROM accounts WHERE id = 1 FOR UPDATE
    DB-->>Buy: Balance = ₹100,000.00
    Note over Buy: Total Cost = 5 * ₹3,500 = ₹17,500.00<br/>Balance >= Total Cost? YES
    
    Buy->>DB: UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 17500.00
    Buy->>DB: UPSERT INTO positions (symbol, qty=5, avg_price=3500.00, sl=3325.00)
    Buy->>DB: INSERT INTO trades (type='BUY', qty=5, price=3500.00, total=17500.00)
    Buy->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
    
    Buy-->>User: Display Success Notice: "Bought 5 shares of TCS.NS"
```

---

### Sequence 4: 24/7 Automated Stop-Loss Trigger & Execution

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Daemon as monitor_stop_loss.py
    participant YF as Yahoo Finance Cloud
    participant API as api/execute_stop_loss.php
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / SQLite
    participant Client as User Browser Dashboard

    loop Every 30 Seconds
        Daemon->>DB: SELECT * FROM positions WHERE stop_loss_price IS NOT NULL
        DB-->>Daemon: Open position: TCS.NS (Qty: 5, SL: ₹3,325.00)
        Daemon->>YF: Fetch real-time price for TCS.NS
        YF-->>Daemon: Real-time price dropped to ₹3,310.00!
        
        Note over Daemon: Trigger Condition Met: ₹3,310.00 <= ₹3,325.00
        
        Daemon->>API: POST /api/execute_stop_loss.php (TCS.NS, trigger_price=3310.00)
        API->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        API->>DB: UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + (5 * 3310.00)
        API->>DB: DELETE FROM positions WHERE symbol = 'TCS.NS'
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO trades (type='SELL', qty=5, price=3310.00, reason='STOP_LOSS_TRIGGERED')
        API->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
        API-->>Daemon: HTTP 200 OK (Executed)
        
        Daemon->>Daemon: Update monitor_heartbeat.json (Last Triggered: TCS.NS)
    end
    
    Client->>API: Periodic status poll / page refresh
    API-->>Client: Returns updated cash balance & trade notification
    Client-->>Client: Show Badge: "Stop-Loss Executed for TCS.NS at ₹3,310.00"
```

---

### Sequence 5: Secure User Logout & Cleanup

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Trader (Browser)
    participant Header as Shared Navigation (header.php)
    participant Logout as Logout Handler (logout.php)
    participant Session as Server Session Manager
    participant Login as Login Page (login.php)

    User->>Header: Click "Logout" Link
    Header->>Logout: GET /logout.php
    Logout->>Logout: Verify Active Session Exists
    Logout->>Session: $_SESSION = [] (Clear memory array)
    Logout->>Logout: setcookie(session_name(), '', time() - 3600, path, domain, secure, httponly)
    Logout->>Session: session_destroy() (Purge server-side session file)
    Logout-->>Login: 302 Redirect to /login.php?status=logged_out
    Login-->>User: Display Login Form with banner: "You have successfully logged out."
```

---

## 8. Failure Handling & Offline Resilience

| Failure Scenario | Automatic System Reaction |
|---|---|
| **PostgreSQL Service Offline** | Seamlessly activates local SQLite storage fallback (`database/simulator.sqlite`). Displays warning banner in UI without crashing user trades. |
| **Yahoo Finance Network Timeout** | Falls back to cached pricing in `price_cache` table. Shows *"Price cached from [timestamp]"* badge in UI. |
| **Stop-Loss Daemon Terminated** | System header displays `🔴 Monitor Inactive` pill. Prevents false assumption of active protection. |
| **Insufficient Virtual Funds** | Atomically rejects order before database commitment. No negative balances permitted (`CHECK (balance >= 0)`). |
| **Invalid Ticker Symbol** | Python validation detects unknown symbol from Yahoo Finance and gracefully returns descriptive error without throwing unhandled exceptions. |
| **Session Invalidation / Expiry** | Expired sessions are intercepted by the `auth_check` middleware and redirected to `login.php` with state preservation. |

